{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"A\n    \n      The Grid Sheet\n      Concept: The page is a strict 12-column grid with visible gridlines. Content snaps to columns. Large uppercase sans-serif headings sit in the left 4 columns, content fills the right 8. Section dividers are thick black horizontal rules. Collapsible sections use a simple [+]/[−] toggle.\n      Typography: One typeface family (e.g., Space Grotesk or Inter) at extreme size contrasts — 72px headings, 14px body.\n      Feel: Like a modernist newspaper or architectural blueprint. Very structured, almost mechanical.\n      Tradeoff: Most visually striking but most rigid — content must fit the grid or it feels broken.","choice":"a","id":null,"timestamp":1774685557150}
{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"B\n    \n      The Specimen Page\n      Concept: Inspired by type specimen sheets. Your name is set massive (100px+) at the top. Below, content is arranged in clearly labeled blocks with heavy borders. Each section is a \"specimen\" — a self-contained card with a bold label. Collapsed sections show only the label bar.\n      Typography: Mix of a grotesque sans-serif for headings and a monospace for body/metadata. Size hierarchy is extreme.\n      Feel: Like a designer's portfolio meets a technical document. Bold but readable.\n      Tradeoff: Most balanced — strong identity without sacrificing readability. Slightly less austere than A.","choice":"b","id":null,"timestamp":1774685558480}
{"source":"user-event","type":"click","text":"C\n    \n      The Index\n      Concept: The page reads like a structured index or table of contents. Minimal decoration — just text, lines, and whitespace. Navigation is a numbered list at the top. Sections are numbered (01, 02, 03...) with thin rule separators. Collapsible sections simply expand inline.\n      Typography: Single monospace typeface throughout. Hierarchy through size and weight only, no style tricks.\n      Feel: Like a terminal output or technical reference. Maximum austerity, almost anti-design.\n      Tradeoff: Most minimal and fastest to build, but risks feeling too plain for a personal homepage.","choice":"c","id":null,"timestamp":1774685559098}
